        "runId": "ada-en-97965d11-b9ef-45cd-a2d6-8f41fb371543",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "Costa Rica: ridged cacao pods among green leaves"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:highlight_title:9549c7a22508099d",
      "field": "highlight.title",
      "sourceTextSha256": "14c11a244a0d76bec3af620cf226eeadaf3a153c380337337c6888452fe03f2c",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-97965d11-b9ef-45cd-a2d6-8f41fb371543",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "An active day near Arenal"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:highlight_text:0d2f65e58aa7868d",
      "field": "highlight.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "c76591ddb434967696d578e0ba969baf5564bc6f57a84bf01999a8a04658617e",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-97965d11-b9ef-45cd-a2d6-8f41fb371543",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "One of the busiest days takes you to the area around Arenal Volcano. First, cross the hanging bridges above the rainforest, then ride the Sky Tram up to the Miguel Ángel lookout.\n\nThe Sky Trek canopy tour features several zip lines covering about 2.8 km in total. Some sections reach a height of 201 m.\n\nAfterwards, you can go canyoning in Lost Canyon, with descents and climbs around six waterfalls. The first waterfall is about 5 m high, and the tallest is around 50 m. Another option is rafting on the Balsa River, with Class II–III rapids. The route covers more than 16 km through a canyon, gorges and stretches with waterfalls."
    },
    {
